{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNoSpacing&quot;&gt;The proposed development, by\r\nreason of its constrained individual dwelling width&#x27;s would appear disproportionately\r\nthin within the wider setting of the surrounding area. The proposed building would fail to adhere\r\nto the wider prevailing streetscene formed of punctured spaces between plots forming a coherent pattern of attractive open building relationships, thereby the development is considered detriment to the character and appearance of\r\nthe street scene. As such, the development is contrary to the high quality design aspirations of the\r\nNational Planning Policy Framework (2023), Policies D3.D(1) and D3.D(11) of The\r\nLondon Plan (2021), Policy CS.1B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policy DM1\r\nof the Development Management Plan Local Policies (2013) and the Adopted\r\nSupplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNoSpacing&quot;&gt;The\r\nproposed four off-street parking spaces located on the frontage of the site\r\nfail to demonstrate the required dimensions to be considered adequate for the\r\nparking of four vehicles. The development has failed to illustrate appropriate\r\npedestrian and cycle access to the two proposed properties and servicing of\r\nrefuse has not been addressed. Considering the substandard parking spaces and access the\r\ndevelopment is considered to result in future conflict and harm to the\r\nfunction of the frontage. As such, the development is contrary to Policies T5,\r\nT6 and of the London Plan (2021), T6.1 and policies DM42 and DM45 of the Harrow\r\nDMP (2013).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
